### Mock hospital scheduling API (Lab 3) – synthetic data only
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" / IntelliJ HTTP client. The JSON files next to this file are
### real request/response pairs captured from the running application.

@base = http://localhost:8083

### 1. Register an availability request (done by job worker triage.request-availability)
POST {{base}}/mock/scheduling/availability-requests
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientReference": "SYN-P-0101",
  "department": "GENERAL_PRACTICE",
  "fromDate": "2026-10-30",
  "toDate": "2026-11-13",
  "timeOfDay": "MORNING",
  "urgencyCategory": "ROUTINE"
}

### 2. Retrieve free slots (this is the call the REST Connector "Retrieve available slots" makes)
GET {{base}}/mock/scheduling/availability-requests/AR-99CD7EE1/slots
Accept: application/json

### 3. Book a slot (done by job worker triage.book-appointment)
POST {{base}}/mock/scheduling/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "availabilityRequestId": "AR-99CD7EE1",
  "slotId": "GEN-20261031-0800",
  "patientReference": "SYN-P-0101"
}

### 4. Fault injection – break the scheduling API (slot query answers HTTP 503)
POST {{base}}/admin/faults/scheduling-api-down?enabled=true

### 5. Fault injection – repair it
POST {{base}}/admin/faults/scheduling-api-down?enabled=false

### 6. Current fault switches
GET {{base}}/admin/faults

### 7. Start a process instance through the Camunda 8 REST API
POST http://localhost:8080/v2/process-instances
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "processDefinitionId": "patient-appointment-triage",
  "variables": {
    "patientReference": "SYN-P-0001",
    "patientAge": 34,
    "appointmentPreference": { "department": "GENERAL_PRACTICE", "preferredDate": "2026-11-03", "timeOfDay": "MORNING" },
    "symptomsSummary": "Mild cough and sore throat for a few days",
    "painLevel": 2,
    "symptomDurationDays": 3
  }
}
